export default [{"s":1.12,"e":5.9,"t":"Episode 1. Where to start reading X-Men without losing your mind."},{"s":5.95,"e":10.56,"t":"A few years ago I walked into Graham Crackers Comics in Chicago as a grown adult and"},{"s":10.61,"e":13.8,"t":"asked the guy behind the counter the most embarrassing question you can ask in a"},{"s":13.85,"e":14.95,"t":"comic shop."},{"s":15,"e":16.94,"t":"Where do I start with X-Men?"},{"s":17.05,"e":22.09,"t":"Because X-Men is 60 years of comics, a dozen books with X-Men in the title and"},{"s":22.14,"e":24.9,"t":"reading orders online that look like tax forms."},{"s":24.95,"e":27.97,"t":"He didn't hand me a reading order, he handed me one book."},{"s":28.02,"e":29.1,"t":"And it worked."},{"s":30.1,"e":32.14,"t":"So that's what this video is."},{"s":32.22,"e":33.49,"t":"Not a reading order."},{"s":33.54,"e":35.35,"t":"Five books. One shelf."},{"s":35.4,"e":36.42,"t":"Let's go."},{"s":37.34,"e":38.35,"t":"Quick background."},{"s":38.4,"e":42.85,"t":"I was eight years old growing up in Chicagoland in 1992 when X-Men the animated"},{"s":42.9,"e":46.2,"t":"series came on and flipped a switch in my brain."},{"s":46.25,"e":51.35,"t":"That theme song still lives rent free and it gets me pumped every single time."},{"s":51.4,"e":53.81,"t":"My best friend is the one who got us all into it."},{"s":53.86,"e":56,"t":"The cartoon, the comics, all of it."},{"s":56.05,"e":59.75,"t":"So he got first pick and he picked Gambit, obviously."},{"s":59.94,"e":62.62,"t":"Gambit and Wolverine were the coolest guys on the show."},{"s":62.72,"e":66.59,"t":"And Gambit had the trench coat, glowing cards and accent none of us could"},{"s":66.64,"e":71.65,"t":"understand. He also decided the girl everybody in class had a crush on was Rogue."},{"s":71.7,"e":72.5,"t":"Kids."},{"s":73.39,"e":74.79,"t":"I got Colossus."},{"s":74.97,"e":76.19,"t":"And I felt cheated."},{"s":76.24,"e":82.01,"t":"Big Russian guy turns into steel says about four words an episode but he was mine so"},{"s":82.06,"e":83.16,"t":"I stuck with him."},{"s":83.21,"e":86.57,"t":"And somewhere along the way I actually started to care about him."},{"s":86.62,"e":88.73,"t":"Strongest guy in the room and he'd rather be home painting."},{"s":88.78,"e":91.88,"t":"I don't think I'm the only one this happened to."},{"s":91.93,"e":93.81,"t":"A lot of us didn't pick our X-Man."},{"s":93.86,"e":96.76,"t":"We got handed one and then we got attached."},{"s":97.19,"e":98.96,"t":"That's how I got into X-Men."},{"s":99.01,"e":101.81,"t":"Not through a reading order, through a character."},{"s":102.09,"e":103.18,"t":"Hold on to that."},{"s":103.23,"e":105.1,"t":"I'm going to come back to it in a minute."},{"s":105.15,"e":107.93,"t":"The obvious move is to start at the beginning."},{"s":108.05,"e":109.48,"t":"X-Men number one."},{"s":109.53,"e":110.39,"t":"1963."},{"s":110.71,"e":112.33,"t":"It matters historically."},{"s":112.49,"e":113.96,"t":"Stan Lee and Jack Kirby."},{"s":114.01,"e":115.43,"t":"The original five."},{"s":115.79,"e":117.45,"t":"Magneto's first appearance."},{"s":117.61,"e":119.58,"t":"Honestly, it feels like a different team."},{"s":119.63,"e":123.4,"t":"But it's good background and it matters more than you'd think once we get to"},{"s":123.45,"e":124.34,"t":"Hickman."},{"s":124.39,"e":126.13,"t":"Hold that thought, too."},{"s":126.49,"e":130.51,"t":"But historically important and a good first read are not the same thing."},{"s":130.56,"e":134.49,"t":"The storytelling has changed a lot in 60 years. And you don't need to do homework to"},{"s":134.54,"e":135.54,"t":"enjoy this stuff."},{"s":135.59,"e":137.66,"t":"So treat it like a tasting menu."},{"s":137.71,"e":139.73,"t":"Five stories from different eras."},{"s":139.85,"e":141.84,"t":"If one grabs you, follow it."},{"s":141.89,"e":143.92,"t":"If one doesn't, skip it."},{"s":143.97,"e":144.77,"t":"Nobody's checking."},{"s":144.8,"e":146.28,"t":"Number one."},{"s":146.38,"e":147.93,"t":"The Dark Phoenix saga."},{"s":147.98,"e":151.06,"t":"Uncanny X-Men 129 through 137."},{"s":151.26,"e":154.03,"t":"1980. Chris Claremont and John Byrne."},{"s":154.08,"e":157.31,"t":"If you only read one X-Men story, it's probably this one."},{"s":157.36,"e":159.43,"t":"It's the team at their peak."},{"s":159.48,"e":162.63,"t":"And it's where a lot of what you know about the X-Men comes from."},{"s":162.68,"e":166.67,"t":"Issue 129 alone introduces Kitty Pryde and Emma Frost."},{"s":166.78,"e":172.76,"t":"130 gives you Dazzler, who's a disco superhero and it's not as corny as it sounds."},{"s":172.96,"e":175.02,"t":"But the real story is Jean Grey."},{"s":175.07,"e":177.63,"t":"She's gained cosmic power."},{"s":177.79,"e":180.99,"t":"The Hellfire Club is introduced and messes with her head."},{"s":181.13,"e":183.3,"t":"And it goes about as well as you'd expect."},{"s":183.35,"e":187.72,"t":"What makes it hold up is that it's not just a big fight like Secret Wars."},{"s":187.77,"e":190.95,"t":"It's a team trying to save a friend from herself."},{"s":191.57,"e":192.83,"t":"And then 137."},{"s":193.17,"e":195.14,"t":"I'm not going to spoil it for you."},{"s":195.19,"e":199.07,"t":"I'll just say it's one of the most famous endings in comics for a reason."},{"s":199.25,"e":203.16,"t":"I've been through the Phoenix story a bunch of times before I ever read the actual"},{"s":203.21,"e":204.15,"t":"book."},{"s":204.21,"e":207.31,"t":"The cartoon did it and honestly did it really well."},{"s":207.39,"e":211.5,"t":"The movies have tried it twice and I'm still waiting for one to get it right."},{"s":211.55,"e":212.69,"t":"But it didn't matter."},{"s":212.74,"e":216.77,"t":"Even knowing how it ends, the trade paperback is still the best way to experience"},{"s":216.82,"e":221.51,"t":"it. Team dynamics, real consequences, and a character arc that people are still"},{"s":221.56,"e":223.45,"t":"adapting 40 years later."},{"s":223.5,"e":225.62,"t":"If you start anywhere, start here."},{"s":225.67,"e":226.69,"t":"Number 2."},{"s":226.79,"e":228.15,"t":"Days of Future Past."},{"s":228.49,"e":231.47,"t":"Uncanny X-Men 141 and 142."},{"s":231.77,"e":232.94,"t":"Short and sweet."},{"s":232.99,"e":235.65,"t":"Two issues. That covers the whole pitch."},{"s":235.7,"e":239.62,"t":"A future where Sentinels won and most of the X-Men are dead or in camps."},{"s":239.67,"e":243.21,"t":"Kitty's mind gets sent back to the present to stop it from happening."},{"s":243.26,"e":247.39,"t":"It's short, it's dark, and it's the blueprint for every stop the bad future story"},{"s":247.44,"e":249.19,"t":"the X-Men have done since."},{"s":249.24,"e":252.4,"t":"Including the movie and the cartoon episode you probably saw first."},{"s":252.45,"e":253.92,"t":"Number 3."},{"s":254.32,"e":255.51,"t":"X-Cutioner's Song."},{"s":255.56,"e":258.08,"t":"This one's for the kids who grew up on the cartoon."},{"s":258.21,"e":262.43,"t":"'92 into '93. A crossover across four X-books."},{"s":262.77,"e":267.68,"t":"Professor X gets shot, Cable's the main suspect, and it turns into a whole mess with"},{"s":267.73,"e":268.72,"t":"Stryfe and Apocalypse."},{"s":268.77,"e":272.17,"t":"It is the most 90s thing you will ever read."},{"s":272.22,"e":275.84,"t":"Everybody's squinting, everybody has pouches, it's pretty rad."},{"s":275.94,"e":279.53,"t":"If the cartoon is your X-Men, this is the comic that feels like it."},{"s":279.58,"e":281.57,"t":"Fair warning, it is messy."},{"s":281.62,"e":284.88,"t":"It jumps across four different books, so grab the trade paperback."},{"s":284.93,"e":286.45,"t":"Puts everything in order for you."},{"s":286.5,"e":287.85,"t":"Number 4."},{"s":287.93,"e":289.63,"t":"God Loves Man Kills."},{"s":289.77,"e":290.97,"t":"1982."},{"s":291.34,"e":293.92,"t":"Chris Claremont and Brent Anderson."},{"s":293.97,"e":295.79,"t":"A standalone graphic novel."},{"s":295.84,"e":297.59,"t":"No continuity homework."},{"s":297.64,"e":299.65,"t":"You pick it up, you read it, you're done."},{"s":299.7,"e":304.15,"t":"A preacher named William Stryker starts a crusade against mutants and the X-Men end"},{"s":304.2,"e":306.1,"t":"up working with Magneto to stop him."},{"s":306.15,"e":309.96,"t":"This is the X-Men that they're most direct about what they've always been about."},{"s":310.01,"e":313.14,"t":"Fear, prejudice, people being hated for what they are."},{"s":313.19,"e":317.05,"t":"It's also the backbone of the second X-Men movie if that's your entry point."},{"s":317.31,"e":320.89,"t":"It's heavy, but it's the one that shows you why these stories still matter."},{"s":321.17,"e":322.86,"t":"Number 5."},{"s":322.91,"e":323.99,"t":"House of M."},{"s":324.13,"e":329.12,"t":"2005. The legendary Brian Michael Bendis and Olivier Coipel."},{"s":329.17,"e":332.08,"t":"This is the book the guy at Graham Crackers handed me."},{"s":332.13,"e":335.33,"t":"The Scarlet Witch rewrites reality."},{"s":335.38,"e":339.05,"t":"Everybody wakes up in a world where they got what they wanted and a few of them"},{"s":339.1,"e":341.22,"t":"start to realize something's wrong."},{"s":341.53,"e":345.83,"t":"It's an event book, so it's big and loud and it touches the Avengers too."},{"s":345.88,"e":350.28,"t":"But it reads clean and it was the perfect way back in for me as a young adult."},{"s":351.26,"e":354.26,"t":"And the ending changed the X-Men for about a decade."},{"s":354.82,"e":357.72,"t":"Three words. You'll know them when you see them."},{"s":358.58,"e":362.25,"t":"Once you've got a few of these under your belt, then read House of X and Powers of"},{"s":362.3,"e":363.99,"t":"X. 2019,"},{"s":364.04,"e":365.19,"t":"Jonathan Hickman."},{"s":365.24,"e":369.39,"t":"It's 12 issues that flip decades of X-Men history on its head."},{"s":369.44,"e":371.19,"t":"Remember X-Men number 1?"},{"s":371.24,"e":374.43,"t":"This is where Xavier's choices, going all the way back to the beginning,"},{"s":374.48,"e":376.16,"t":"start catching up with him."},{"s":376.34,"e":377.21,"t":"It's brilliant."},{"s":377.26,"e":378.13,"t":"And it's also a lot."},{"s":378.18,"e":381.89,"t":"It lands so much harder when you know who these people are and what they've been"},{"s":381.94,"e":383.49,"t":"through. So don't start there."},{"s":383.54,"e":385.86,"t":"Save it. It'll be waiting."},{"s":386.2,"e":388.1,"t":"And here's my actual advice."},{"s":388.38,"e":389.47,"t":"Shop like a kid."},{"s":389.52,"e":392.46,"t":"When you were 10, you didn't need a reading order."},{"s":392.51,"e":396.53,"t":"You grabbed whatever cover looked cool and figured it out."},{"s":396.58,"e":397.93,"t":"Find a character you like."},{"s":397.98,"e":400.95,"t":"For me it was Colossus and I didn't even pick him."},{"s":401,"e":402.54,"t":"For you it might be Storm."},{"s":402.59,"e":403.96,"t":"Then you can follow them."},{"s":404.01,"e":408.59,"t":"Read their stories, jump around, get confused, look stuff up."},{"s":408.71,"e":410.07,"t":"That's half the fun."},{"s":410.34,"e":414.81,"t":"Quick note. I built ComixCatalog because I wanted one place to track what I own"},{"s":414.86,"e":416.24,"t":"and what I'm hunting."},{"s":416.32,"e":419.81,"t":"You can search any of these books, see the covers, and throw the ones you want on a"},{"s":419.86,"e":424.3,"t":"wantlist so you're not standing in a shop trying to remember issue numbers."},{"s":424.5,"e":425.83,"t":"It's free to use."},{"s":425.88,"e":428,"t":"Link's below. So the shelf."},{"s":428.42,"e":433.93,"t":"Dark Phoenix, Days of Future Past, X-Cutioner's Song, God Loves Man Kills,"},{"s":433.98,"e":435.18,"t":"and House of M."},{"s":435.46,"e":438.2,"t":"And then House of X and Powers of X when you're ready."},{"s":438.25,"e":440.63,"t":"Don't turn reading comics into homework."},{"s":440.68,"e":444.24,"t":"Go pick up a comic and come back and tell me which one you started with."}];
